    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0390" n="316" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/714</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-12-15T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 15, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1689. Your 59, November 17,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d308-f1"/> and subsequent
                    telegrams on situation. Department appreciates your sound and able handling of
                    difficult conditions, also courageous cooperation of your staff, including
                    Poole. No Government either belligerent or neutral has recognized Bolshevik
                    government at Petrograd.</p>
                <p>Department desires to keep in close touch with developments [in] Moscow and
                    Moscow district.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
